276
00:16:51,347 --> 00:16:53,347
Hmm...

277
00:16:53,347 --> 00:16:54,347
Damn it!

278
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:56,347
We've got enough problems.

279
00:16:56,347 --> 00:16:59,347
We don't need this guy giving us one more thing to worry about!

280
00:16:59,347 --> 00:17:00,347
Don't get worked up.

281
00:17:00,347 --> 00:17:03,347
It's not like he's an actual threat to any of us.

282
00:17:03,347 --> 00:17:04,347
Hehehehe.

283
00:17:04,347 --> 00:17:05,347
That's right.

284
00:17:05,347 --> 00:17:06,347
You think that.

285
00:17:06,347 --> 00:17:19,347
You'll see how wrong you are now that the three morons who could put up a fight have gotten themselves killed fighting that kraken.

286
00:17:19,347 --> 00:17:20,347
Hehehehe.

287
00:17:20,347 --> 00:17:27,347
After all, there's no way they survived getting sucked down into the bowels of the ocean with just those tiny bubbles to protect them.

288
00:17:27,347 --> 00:17:28,347
Huh?

289
00:17:28,347 --> 00:17:41,347
What a shame I didn't have the chance to kill Straw Hat with my own hands.

290
00:17:41,347 --> 00:17:48,347
But no one will ever doubt that he's dead once I come back with the rest of his crew members' heads in tow as my personal trophies.

291
00:17:48,347 --> 00:17:50,347
No one at all.

292
00:17:50,347 --> 00:17:51,347
Hehehehe.

293
00:17:51,347 --> 00:17:54,347
But I can't get too excited.

294
00:17:54,347 --> 00:17:56,347
There's no need to rush.

295
00:17:56,347 --> 00:18:00,347
If I killed them all now, there wouldn't be anyone left to sail the ship.

296
00:18:00,347 --> 00:18:01,347
And then what would I do?

297
00:18:01,347 --> 00:18:05,347
So I'll let them live for now while they can still be useful to me.

298
00:18:05,347 --> 00:18:11,347
Once we land on Fishman Island, though, I'm gonna slaughter you down to the last man.

299
00:18:11,347 --> 00:18:13,347
Hehehehe.

300
00:18:13,347 --> 00:18:14,347
I found him, guys!

301
00:18:14,347 --> 00:18:15,347
Hey!

302
00:18:15,347 --> 00:18:16,347
Not knocking off, dammit!

303
00:18:16,347 --> 00:18:17,347
I wasn't doing anything bad!

304
00:18:17,347 --> 00:18:18,347
I swear!

305
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,347
Let's see him break out of that.

306
00:18:19,347 --> 00:18:33,487
I found him, guys!

307
00:18:33,727 --> 00:18:35,767
Hey! Not knocking off, dammit!

308
00:18:35,907 --> 00:18:37,947
I wasn't doing anything bad, I swear!

309
00:18:38,427 --> 00:18:39,747
Let's see him break out of that.

310
00:18:40,007 --> 00:18:42,067
How did he even manage to get in there?

311
00:18:42,547 --> 00:18:44,387
Because we weren't paying attention to him.

312
00:18:44,727 --> 00:18:46,967
If he weren't so stupid, we could have been in trouble.

313
00:18:46,967 --> 00:18:49,807
His body was like a big mass of goo in there.

314
00:18:49,927 --> 00:18:50,967
It didn't have a real shape.

315
00:18:51,207 --> 00:18:52,647
So he was like a pile of mud?

316
00:18:52,767 --> 00:18:55,227
Yeah, if I had to guess, it's a devil fruit power.

317
00:18:55,847 --> 00:18:58,067
Most likely a Logia-type fruit at that.

318
00:18:58,347 --> 00:19:00,487
He was giving us a false sense of security,

319
00:19:00,707 --> 00:19:02,587
because he could have escaped at any time.

320
00:19:02,707 --> 00:19:05,187
Get me out of here! I'll behave, I swear!

321
00:19:05,507 --> 00:19:06,987
You and the banana hammock!

322
00:19:07,207 --> 00:19:09,067
If you let me out, I'll be your servant!

323
00:19:09,527 --> 00:19:10,367
Come on!

324
00:19:10,367 --> 00:19:17,107
You feeling all right, Chopper?

325
00:19:17,627 --> 00:19:18,587
I don't know.

326
00:19:18,967 --> 00:19:20,527
It just got really hot.

327
00:19:21,207 --> 00:19:22,687
I can't stand the heat.

328
00:19:23,107 --> 00:19:23,907
I'm dying.

329
00:19:24,827 --> 00:19:25,427
Sheesh!

330
00:19:25,787 --> 00:19:26,707
It is warmer.

331
00:19:27,707 --> 00:19:28,767
Wait a second.

332
00:19:29,027 --> 00:19:29,867
Is that smoke?

333
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:31,887
We can't see what's in front of us through that!

334
00:19:34,027 --> 00:19:35,347
Smoke under the wire?

335
00:19:35,887 --> 00:19:36,727
Can't be.

336
00:19:36,727 --> 00:19:38,207
Actually, it can.

337
00:19:39,547 --> 00:19:40,727
Is that...

338
00:19:42,727 --> 00:19:47,847
Hydrothermal deposits!

339
00:19:48,127 --> 00:19:48,367
What?

340
00:19:48,907 --> 00:19:49,627
Keep up!

341
00:19:49,807 --> 00:19:51,207
This is a volcanic area!

342
00:19:51,567 --> 00:19:52,207
For real?

343
00:19:52,587 --> 00:19:53,547
Yes, for real!

344
00:19:53,887 --> 00:19:55,667
You can see where there have been eruptions!

345
00:19:55,987 --> 00:19:57,427
We have to get out of here now!

346
00:19:57,907 --> 00:19:59,887
If one of those erupts, we're as good as dead!

347
00:20:00,967 --> 00:20:01,987
It's hot.

348
00:20:02,187 --> 00:20:03,287
I'm so hot.

349
00:20:04,247 --> 00:20:04,647
Ugh.

350
00:20:05,447 --> 00:20:05,847
Ugh.

351
00:20:06,727 --> 00:20:08,307
There's something coming after us!

352
00:20:08,567 --> 00:20:10,267
It's carnivorous tube worms!

353
00:20:10,407 --> 00:20:11,327
Got no choice.

354
00:20:11,787 --> 00:20:12,447
Small one.

355
00:20:12,947 --> 00:20:13,947
Coup de burst!

356
00:20:16,147 --> 00:20:16,507
No!

357
00:20:18,087 --> 00:20:19,147
Traceless crabs!

358
00:20:20,187 --> 00:20:21,527
Have to risk it again!

359
00:20:21,767 --> 00:20:22,587
Coup de burst!

360
00:20:22,687 --> 00:20:23,087
Ah!

361
00:20:23,967 --> 00:20:26,167
I don't even know what the hell those things are!

362
00:20:26,227 --> 00:20:27,027
Hang on, guys!

363
00:20:27,407 --> 00:20:28,207
Coup de burst!

364
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:30,207
The sea is awful!

365
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:31,187
I hate it!

366
00:20:31,767 --> 00:20:35,227
There's no way the others can survive down here on their own!

367
00:20:35,227 --> 00:20:37,727
I can't believe this is happening!

368
00:20:38,087 --> 00:20:39,907
And we'd only just gotten back together!

369
00:20:40,027 --> 00:20:40,907
Stop crying!

370
00:20:41,107 --> 00:20:43,207
Those three are way too tough to die!

371
00:20:43,587 --> 00:20:48,247
Even using Coup de burst that sparingly, we've lost so much air already!

372
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:53,307
What is that?

373
00:20:53,307 --> 00:20:54,087
A light?

374
00:20:54,207 --> 00:20:54,927
In the darkness?

375
00:20:55,707 --> 00:20:56,047
Wait!

376
00:20:56,587 --> 00:20:57,647
Is that Fishman Island?

377
00:20:58,387 --> 00:21:00,027
Maybe Luffy beat us there!

378
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:01,227
It can't be!

379
00:21:01,307 --> 00:21:03,447
We haven't descended the last 3,000 meters!

380
00:21:03,547 --> 00:21:04,607
Who are you?

381
00:21:04,907 --> 00:21:05,707
A friend?

382
00:21:06,467 --> 00:21:06,987
Stop!

383
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:09,687
If you want to flash signals, do it without actually flashing!

384
00:21:10,467 --> 00:21:11,447
Can you tell what it is?

385
00:21:11,447 --> 00:21:13,467
No, it's still too bright to see!

386
00:21:16,147 --> 00:21:17,587
Oh no!

387
00:21:20,787 --> 00:21:22,267
An anglerfish!

388
00:21:22,567 --> 00:21:23,347
We're screwed!

389
00:21:24,247 --> 00:21:27,427
The deep sea hunter fooled us hook, line, and sinker!

390
00:21:30,587 --> 00:21:32,327
A little close that time!

391
00:21:32,487 --> 00:21:34,187
There isn't anywhere left for us to run!

392
00:21:34,807 --> 00:21:35,847
What can we do?

393
00:21:35,847 --> 00:21:44,187
This can't be happening!

394
00:21:44,707 --> 00:21:45,847
It's human?

395
00:21:46,107 --> 00:21:47,807
No, this doesn't make any sense!

396
00:21:48,227 --> 00:21:49,247
A sea monster?

397
00:21:49,787 --> 00:21:52,007
That's taking the form of a man!

398
00:21:53,147 --> 00:21:55,207
It's a sea monster!

399
00:22:00,007 --> 00:22:02,047
He's going to cat-size the ship!

400
00:22:02,047 --> 00:22:07,667
What the?

401
00:22:08,047 --> 00:22:09,367
Hey, that's naughty!

402
00:22:09,727 --> 00:22:11,207
You know better, Ancaro!

403
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:14,167
You're not allowed to eat ships!

404
00:22:14,967 --> 00:22:17,107
How many times do I have to tell you?

405
00:22:18,327 --> 00:22:21,827
Captain Vander Decken won't be happy when he hears about this!

406
00:22:21,947 --> 00:22:24,087
Wait, did he just help us?

407
00:22:24,827 --> 00:22:26,167
Who freaking cares?

408
00:22:26,347 --> 00:22:27,787
Let's just make a break for it!

409
00:22:27,887 --> 00:22:29,327
He might change his mind!

410
00:22:29,327 --> 00:22:32,567
He might change his mind!

411
00:22:32,567 --> 00:22:33,487
Ohhhh!

412
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:37,587
Aaaaaahhhhhh!

413
00:22:38,967 --> 00:22:39,887
O-o-o-o-o-o-o!

414
00:22:42,447 --> 00:22:42,927
Gah!

415
00:22:43,047 --> 00:22:44,367
Please no more!

416
00:22:51,887 --> 00:22:54,907
O-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o!

417
00:22:54,907 --> 00:23:15,227
The legendary ghost ship the Flying Dutchman emerges from the darkness, closing in on the horrified Straw Hats.

418
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:21,707
However, before they encounter its creepy captain, a volcano erupts, sending them diving into a trench.

419
00:23:21,707 --> 00:23:26,707
What they find there is not the seafloor, but another deadly nightmare.

420
00:23:26,707 --> 00:23:34,707
On the next One Piece, undersea volcanic eruption, drifting to the Fishman Island, I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

